WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
Let's do a few together.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.746
Problem 1.

00:00:03.796 --> 00:00:08.332
A gold strip is 1 foot 2 inches long and 2 inches wide.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:10.562
How many gold sheets cover it?

00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:12.976
Are the lengths in the same units?

00:00:13.026 --> 00:00:14.195
No.

00:00:14.245 --> 00:00:18.596
One side is in feet and inches, and the other is in inches.

00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:22.299
1 foot is 12 inches, and 2 more is 14.

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:24.888
So the strip is 14 inches long.

00:00:24.938 --> 00:00:26.967
One row of 14 sheets.

00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.499
And there are 2 rows.

00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:31.471
14 times 2 is 28.

00:00:31.521 --> 00:00:34.154
The area is 28 square inches.

00:00:34.204 --> 00:00:35.721
Problem 2.

00:00:35.771 --> 00:00:37.486
Your turn first.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.564
Pause the video and try this one.

00:00:39.614 --> 00:00:41.758
Then press play and check.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.904
A rug is 3 yards long and 2 feet wide.

00:00:44.954 --> 00:00:47.331
Find the area in square feet.

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:51.406
1 yard is 3 feet, so 3 yards is 9 feet.

00:00:51.456 --> 00:00:53.948
9 times 2 is 18.

00:00:53.998 --> 00:00:56.746
The area is 18 square feet.

00:00:56.796 --> 00:00:58.244
Problem 3.

00:00:58.294 --> 00:01:00.020
Watch out for this one.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.492
A lid is 1 foot long and 7 inches wide.

00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:06.650
Someone wrote 1 times 7 is 7.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.238
The times table is right, but the units are mixed.

00:01:10.288 --> 00:01:12.885
Change 1 foot to 12 inches.

00:01:12.935 --> 00:01:15.764
12 times 7 is 84.

00:01:15.814 --> 00:01:19.375
The area is 84 square inches.

00:01:19.425 --> 00:01:23.961
Ask it every time: are the lengths in the same units?
